id: pm-jev-3ntg
title: Propose typed relationship edges with the local decision model
description: "Add bounded typed relationship proposals, guarded SDK dependency application, streaming backlog mode, real-tracker regression proofs and local model acceptance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-15T18:02:27.335Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T18:36:27.146Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T18:02:43.124Z",codex-agent,"Design: reuse certified complete reads and deterministic dedupe ranking; resolve relationship kinds and graph directions through the pinned host SDK. Ask one typed choice per candidate in one bounded request. Guard source revisions inside the host item lock and submit dependency additions plus one redacted receipt in one update. Default dry runs remain observational; hierarchy writes require explicit opt-in. Real tracker tests, independent behavioural mutants, and disposable local tev1:4b acceptance precede unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-15T18:08:52.714Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses the host dependency flag format id=<id>,kind=<kind> in the same update as one receipt. SDK inspection confirms eleven canonical supported kinds and no duplicate kind. First real-tracker regressions cover inverse and symmetric existing edges, scalar parents, hierarchy opt-in, thresholds, abstention, corrupt complete reads and lock guard expiry. Host gap: pinned SDK list/get reads write disposable runtime metadata caches and context usage; no public per-call suppression exists. Dry-run proofs compare every authoritative item, history, schema and settings file, excluding only host runtime files. No protected host source or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-15T18:15:19.901Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs: independently replacing only the relationship apply guard with an unconditional write makes the dry-run authoritative-file hash regression exit 1. Independently disabling existingLinkKinds membership makes the real-tracker existing-edge regression exit 1. Each mutant changes only decideLinks; tests import source, so no dist rebuild is needed. Source restored byte-for-byte (SHA256 d3c07c1a38b04cf6780241bedcb8f2f891d1734140c5966bb3d50fdba8880662); focused dry-run and existing-edge tests then pass 2/2. No mutant retained. Initial real-model request failed safely because a prompt exceeded the local 2050-token input bound. Compact SDK-derived ontology criteria preserve label semantics; the same six-candidate diagnostic now succeeds. Packed-host acceptance is rerunning before final evidence is recorded."
  "2026-10-15T18:17:24.712Z",codex-agent,"Packed real-host acceptance passed 1/1 against local tev1:4b: eight synthetic items, six candidates, one request, 42453 ms CLI latency, 10458 input and 7 output tokens. Top judgments: tests child p=0.385361; research child p=0.209537 abstained; rollout blocks p=0.629304; documentation related p=0.293816; security epic parent p=0.565559; migration blocked_by p=0.537797 existing edge excluded. No proposal qualified at 0.8. All authoritative tracker files stayed byte-identical, no receipt was added, and the installed host rejected an expired receipt. docs/link-proposals.md records uncertainty, input limits and the host runtime-write limitation. Focused real-tracker tests passed 13/13; a further missing-source failure regression passes 1/1. Full unchanged gates follow."
  "2026-10-15T18:26:34.597Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm and Bun gates each ran 167 tests: 166 passed and one existing triage failure exposed a shared-helper regression. The host command result contract requires exit_code, not exitCode; the helper now preserves the original snake-case contract. Coverage already measured 100 percent in every dimension. Link backlog tests now assert the actual harness exit status, and packed-host acceptance additionally requests a nonexistent local model to prove exit 1 without authoritative writes. Both full gates and linked tests will be rerun after this correction; failed gates are not counted as passes."
  "2026-10-15T18:27:54.273Z",codex-agent,"Post-correction verification: the existing triage failure-continuation test plus link backlog exit-status and missing-source tests pass 3/3. Both independent decideLinks mutants were rerun: dry-run bypass exits 1; existing-edge bypass exits 1. Restored source SHA256 is 99453c8138e88981aec8f0276d58900e2967f070eb0f9f31a63d5c219e27e0a7; restored focused revert regressions pass 2/2. Typecheck, test compilation and zero-duplication checks pass. The final linked runner uses tracker context because source-workspace execution cannot use pm-context none; no project policy was changed."
  "2026-10-15T18:36:22.653Z",codex-agent,"Final linked verification passed 4/4 commands with isolated HOME and Git configuration: focused real-tracker tests 14/14; npm release:check 167/167; Bun release:check 167/167; packed real-host acceptance 1/1. Both full gates have zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos, 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines across all 12 authored sources, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, current changelog and valid publication attestation. Final tev1:4b repeat: 8 items, 6 candidates, 67033 ms, 10458 input/7 output tokens. Tests and documentation abstain; research blocked_by p=0.300705; rollout blocks p=0.500356; epic parent p=0.669761 requires opt-in; existing migration blocked_by p=0.820882 is excluded. No new edge qualifies. Authoritative tracker hashes stay identical; actual installed host exits 1 on a missing model and refuses an expired receipt. Source SHA256 remains 99453c8138e88981aec8f0276d58900e2967f070eb0f9f31a63d5c219e27e0a7. Host gaps/constraints: SDK read-side runtime cache and usage writes cannot be disabled per call; universal read-output flags are unavailable on pm test; source-workspace pm-context none is refused. Automatic test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so these receipts are comments. No dependency, threshold or release policy changed. Claim will be released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
